<report>
<title>Risk analysis (prospective)</title>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><td></td><td><subtotal>Characteristic factor:</subtotal></td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td><subtotal>Outcome:</subtotal></td><td>Present</td><td>Absent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Positive</td><td><in>a_out</in></td><td><in>b_out</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Negative</td><td><in>c_out</in></td><td><in>d_out</in></td></tr>
</table>
<line></line>
<line>Risk ratio (relative risk in incidence study) = <inu>ratio</inu></line>
<line><ci>Approximate (Koopman) <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <inu>koopman_from</inu> to <inu>koopman_to</inu></ci></line>
<line>Approximate power <in>pwr</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>Risk difference = <inu>dif</inu></line>
<line><ci>Approximate (Miettinen) <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <inu>miettinen_from</inu> to <inu>miettinen_to</inu></ci></line>
<block name="exposure">
<line></line>
<line>Population exposure % = <inu>pe</inu></line>
<line>Population attributable risk % = <inu>par</inu></line>
<line><ci>Approximate (Walter) <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <inu>walter_from</inu> to <inu>walter_to</inu></ci></line>
</block>
</report>